Implement:

## One-Time Enrollment Token

An administrator creates an enrollment request in Agent Center.

The backend generates:

```text
Enrollment ID
One-time enrollment token
Expiration
Tenant ID
Allowed agent role
Allowed environment
Optional device constraints
```

Example lifecycle:

```text
Administrator
     │
     ▼
Agent Center
     │
     ▼
Create Enrollment
     │
     ▼
Short-lived token
     │
     ▼
Installer
     │
     ▼
Enrollment API
     │
     ▼
Validate token
     │
     ▼
Bind endpoint
     │
     ▼
Issue permanent agent identity
     │
     ▼
Immediately invalidate enrollment token
```

Enrollment tokens should:

* expire quickly
* be single-use
* be tenant-scoped
* be role-scoped
* optionally be IP/network scoped
* optionally be device-bound
* be revocable
* be fully audited

Never store plaintext enrollment tokens in database records if avoidable.

Store a secure hash/fingerprint for verification.

